Here is the updated Frontend Dashboard code. We will integrate Chart.js via CDN into your public/index.html file to convert the incoming data stream into a live, real-time scrolling line chart.

🌐 Updated Frontend with Live Chart (public/index.html)

Replace your existing public/index.html file with the code below. This setup maintains a dynamic dataset of the last 20 data points to prevent the browser from lagging.
html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Live Telemetry Dashboard with Chart</title>
    <!-- Include Socket.io and Chart.js via CDN -->
    <script src="/socket.io/socket.io.js"></script>
    <script src="https://jsdelivr.net"></script>
    <style>
        body { 
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif; 
            background: #121214; 
            color: #e4e4e7; 
            padding: 30px;
            margin: 0;
        }
        .container {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 20px;
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }
        .card { 
            background: #1a1a1e; 
            padding: 25px; 
            border-radius: 12px; 
            box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.4); 
            border: 1px solid #2e2e33;
        }
        .metrics-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
            gap: 15px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        .metric-box {
            background: #222227;
            padding: 15px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            border: 1px solid #2e2e33;
        }
        .metric-box small { color: #a1a1aa; font-size: 0.85rem; }
        .metric-box h3 { margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.4rem; }
        .chart-container {
            position: relative;
            height: 350px;
            width: 100%;
        }
        .green { color: #4caf50; } 
        .red { color: #f44336; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="container">
        <h1>📊 Live Market Telemetry Dashboard (GDP)</h1>
        
        <!-- Live Metrics Cards -->
        <div class="card">
            <div class="metrics-grid">
                <div class="metric-box">
                    <small>Country Code</small>
                    <h3 id="country">-</h3>
                </div>
                <div class="metric-box">
                    <small>Simulated Market Price</small>
                    <h3 id="price">$0.00</h3>
                </div>
                <div class="metric-box">
                    <small>Live Variance</small>
                    <h3 id="variance">-</h3>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div style="text-align: right;">
                <small style="color: #71717a;">Last updated: <span id="time">-</span></small>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Real-Time Chart Visual -->
        <div class="card">
            <h3>Market Price Over Time</h3>
            <div class="chart-container">
                <canvas id="liveChart"></canvas>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        // 1. Initialize Chart.js configuration
        const ctx = document.getElementById('liveChart').getContext('2d');
        const MAX_DATA_POINTS = 20;

        const liveChart = new Chart(ctx, {
            type: 'line',
            data: {
                labels: [], // Timestamps go here
                datasets: [{
                    label: 'Market Price (USD)',
                    data: [], // Numerical price stream values go here
                    borderColor: '#3b82f6',
                    backgroundColor: 'rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.1)',
                    borderWidth: 2,
                    tension: 0.3, // Curve smoothing
                    fill: true,
                    pointRadius: 3,
                    pointHoverRadius: 6
                }]
            },
            options: {
                responsive: true,
                maintainAspectRatio: false,
                scales: {
                    x: {
                        grid: { color: '#2e2e33' },
                        ticks: { color: '#a1a1aa' }
                    },
                    y: {
                        grid: { color: '#2e2e33' },
                        ticks: { color: '#a1a1aa' }
                    }
                },
                plugins: {
                    legend: { display: false }
                }
            }
        });

        // 2. Connect to local Node.js Socket.io Server
        const socket = io();

        socket.on('dashboard_update', (payload) => {
            const telemetry = payload.data;
            if (!telemetry) return;

            const timeString = new Date().toLocaleTimeString();
            const currentPrice = Number(telemetry.simulated_market_price);

            // A. Update HTML text nodes
            document.getElementById('country').innerText = telemetry.country_code || 'N/A';
            document.getElementById('price').innerText = '$' + currentPrice.toLocaleString();
            
            const varianceEl = document.getElementById('variance');
            const vVal = telemetry.live_variance;
            varianceEl.innerText = (vVal > 0 ? '+' : '') + vVal + '%';
            varianceEl.className = vVal >= 0 ? 'green' : 'red';
            document.getElementById('time').innerText = timeString;

            // B. Push data to the chart timeline arrays
            liveChart.data.labels.push(timeString);
            liveChart.data.datasets[0].data.push(currentPrice);

            // C. Maintain scrolling limit window (sliding array mechanism)
            if (liveChart.data.labels.length > MAX_DATA_POINTS) {
                liveChart.data.labels.shift();
                liveChart.data.datasets[0].data.shift();
            }

            // D. Render chart update visually
            liveChart.update();
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
Use code with caution.

📊 Full Stack UI Component Overview


Layer Segment	Technology Applied	Functional Role on Event Lifecycle
Backend Stream Client	ws (WebSocket Protocol)	Pulls continuous market variations from sazwan.digital.
Persistence Database	mongoose (BSON Schema)	Stores data immutable history chunks into your local MongoDB.
Pub/Sub Broker	socket.io (Server Instance)	Broadcasts incoming stream chunks instantly to active client browsers.
Dynamic Frontend	Vanilla JavaScript DOM	Updates text-based UI statistics on individual ticks.
Visual Core Rendering	Chart.js v4 API	Shifts line paths gracefully as updates occur to generate a scrolling dynamic timeline graph.

